+# Unplug Control Centre — Phase 9: Advertising & Banner Campaign Manager
+
+## Purpose
+Turn the existing rotating `ad_slots` banner feature into an operational advertising campaign manager without replacing the public banner renderer or mixing it with the separate Participation Engine sponsor-campaign product.
+
+## Database migration
+Run `unplug-backend/db/migrations/186_ad_banner_campaign_manager.sql` before starting the new backend.
+
+The migration adds campaign/advertiser metadata, recorded value/payment state, safe archive state, and daily aggregate banner analytics (`ad_banner_analytics`). Existing paid banners inherit payment value/status where possible.
+
+## Admin changes
+Advertising → **Banner Campaigns** now includes:
+- summary cards for live/scheduled/pending/value/impressions/clicks/CTR;
+- campaign/advertiser/contact search;
+- All / Live / Scheduled / Paused / Expired / Pending / Archived filters;
+- full campaign editor with placement-specific creative requirements;
+- desktop + optional mobile creative;
+- campaign dates, rotation/effect/duration, target URL and CTA;
+- recorded value + payment status (Finance Manage / Super Admin only);
+- impressions, clicks and CTR per campaign;
+- Archive / Restore instead of normal destructive deletion.
+
+Existing **Paid Banner Submissions Awaiting Approval** remains connected to the member checkout and approval/refund-to-credit workflow.
+
+## Public tracking
+The public `/page-cms` response now exposes the public campaign id (`id`) for banner slots.
+
+New anonymous endpoints:
+- `POST /ad-banners/:id/impression`
+- `GET /ad-banners/:id/click`
+
+No viewer id, member id, fingerprint or visitor IP is stored in `ad_banner_analytics`; the table stores aggregate daily counts by campaign.
+
+The public carousel records an impression when a real banner becomes visible and de-duplicates that banner for the current page-CMS render in the browser. Clicks use the first-party tracking endpoint, which increments and validates the destination before redirecting.
+
+## Permissions / finance boundary
+Campaign creative/schedule/advertiser management requires `advertising.manage`.
+
+Reading or changing `amount_paid` / `payment_status` requires finance access:
+- read: `finance.view`
+- edit: `finance.manage`
+
+The server strips finance fields from advertising-only staff and preserves current financial values when such a user saves the rest of a campaign.
+
+`/page-cms/admin/ad-slots*` is explicitly mapped to advertising permission rather than Pages/Layout permission.
+
+## Reporting/search integration
+Phase 8 Business Reports now includes:
+- banner impressions;
+- banner clicks;
+- banner CTR;
+- export rows for those metrics.
+
+Universal Search banner results now search campaign name, advertiser, contact name/email, placement/link and return the real numeric slot id for navigation.
+
+## Compatibility
+- The public banner renderer still reads the same `ad_slots` table.
+- The existing `GET /ad-banners` remains available for public reads.
+- The existing DELETE route remains for backwards compatibility but the new Control Centre uses Archive/Restore.
+- Participation Engine Sponsor Campaigns remain a separate product for larger sponsored missions/rankings/"presented by" partnerships.
+
+## Validation completed
+- `node --check` passed for all changed/new backend JS files.
+- Admin Dashboard main script passed `node --check` after extraction.
+- Public Magazine main script passed `node --check` after extraction.
+- Permission smoke mapping confirms `/page-cms/admin/ad-slots` → `advertising.manage` while genuine page CMS management → `pages.manage`.
