+# Unplug Control Centre — Production Rollback Plan
+
+Use only after staging approval and a production deploy decision.
+
+## Before production deploy
+Record:
+- Git commit/branch that is currently live on Cloudflare.
+- Render deployment id/commit currently live.
+- Timestamped PostgreSQL backup reference.
+- Current `/health` and `/health/ready` responses.
+- Current revenue/payment reconciliation totals.
+
+## Rollback triggers
+Rollback application code if any of the following appears after deploy:
+- Admin cannot sign in.
+- Member sign-in/verification is broadly broken.
+- `/health/ready` fails after previously being healthy.
+- Confirmed payments fail to fulfil broadly.
+- Public content becomes unavailable.
+- CSP/CORS prevents normal frontend/API communication.
+- Staff can access unauthorized Finance/System functions.
+- Unexpected destructive content/media behaviour occurs.
+
+## Application rollback order
+1. Pause production code changes.
+2. Roll Render back to the recorded previous healthy deployment/commit.
+3. Roll Cloudflare Pages back to the recorded previous healthy deployment.
+4. Verify `/health`, `/health/ready`, Admin, public site and member login.
+5. Reconcile payments made during the deploy window before changing any payment/service statuses.
+
+## Database rule
+Do **not** automatically delete the Control Centre's additive tables/columns during an application rollback. Older code can normally ignore them and keeping the schema avoids destructive rollback risk.
+
+Restore the production database only if there is verified data corruption that cannot be corrected safely. A database restore can erase valid registrations, payments, votes, submissions and edits created after the backup.
+
+## Payment rule
+Never mass-change confirmed payments back to pending as part of rollback. Preserve payment evidence and use Checkout Health/manual reconciliation for affected fulfilment.
+
+## Audit rule
+Preserve `activity_log`, payment rows and fulfilment errors for the incident investigation.
+
+## Resume
+Fix in staging, repeat the failed smoke test plus adjacent journeys, and create a new deployment candidate. Do not "fix forward" directly on production without testing.
